# AGENTS.md — agent-platform

This repository is the canonical source for the provider-neutral agent platform.
Legacy repositories and runtime directories are migration evidence, not governing
instructions.

## Authority

- GitHub Issues define intent, dependencies, and acceptance criteria.
- Git objects identify source state. Receipts bind artifacts, checks, and reviews to
  exact inputs and candidates.
- Runtime sessions, chat, dashboards, semantic memory, and transcripts are supporting
  views, not execution authority.

## Cold start

Read [`docs/START-HERE.md`](docs/START-HERE.md) first before planning, claiming,
implementing, or asserting current platform state. It is the canonical cold-start
source of truth and routes current drift prevention to the delivery ledger.

## Work

- Inspect current status and relevant files before changing anything; preserve
  unrelated work.
- Give each concurrent mutating attempt its own writable workspace and one path owner.
- Keep contracts and source here. Keep credentials, sessions, caches, databases,
  provider profiles, model files, and large run artifacts outside this repository.
- Adopt legacy material only through an explicit issue and current verification.
- Apply [`docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md`](docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md) to every effect. An
  admitted controller-authorized `AUTO_WRITE` does not require a fresh interactive
  request; `APPROVAL_DESTRUCTIVE` does and must carry its valid approval grant.

## Evidence

- Run focused deterministic checks before model review.
- The generator is not the judge; material candidates require fresh independent review.
- Distinguish projected, discovered, loaded, activated, and behaviorally verified state.
- Fail closed on stale revisions, ambiguous ownership, drift, or missing provenance.
- Work level controls ceremony only:
  - L0 is an owning-issue `PATTERN-CANDIDATE` observation comment with no
    correction. L0 is observation/comment only: no branch, pull request, or
    review.
  - L1 is a nonmaterial correction with focused deterministic checks/CI. L1
    is a bounded nonmaterial correction with a focused falsifier test and
    ordinary CI; it has no heavyweight independent model review unless the
    Operating Model separately requires it.
  - L2 is material code, architecture, or security work. L2 material code,
    architecture, or security work requires affected integration tests, one
    independent exact-head review, and expected-head promotion only when the
    Operating Model authorizes it.
  Deterministic CI remains cheap automatic evidence. Review must not expand
  into unrelated hardening.
  [`docs/DELIVERY-FAILURE-LEDGER.md`](docs/DELIVERY-FAILURE-LEDGER.md) is the
  sole canonical proportional anti-pattern register.
- Work level never grants authority and cannot waive any authorization or
  review gate; [`docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md`](docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md) controls
  effect authorization.

Read [`docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md`](docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md) before classifying an effect.
Read `docs/MASTER-PLAN.md` before planning or claiming platform work. Read
`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` when changing platform boundaries. Read migration evidence only
when an issue explicitly imports or retires legacy material.
